  "body": "- Updated Mesa3D to [26.2.6](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/blob/26.2/docs/relnotes/26.2.6.rst?ref_type=heads&plain=0).\r\n- ARM64 binaries are provided by mmozeiko [here](https://github.com/mmozeiko/build-mesa/tags).\r\n- Support for x86 32-bit build in MinGW has been restored but without LLVM support to workaround [#156](https://github.com/pal1000/mesa-dist-win/issues/156) so no openclon12, llvmpipe or lavapipe and performance is much lower for software fallback emulated features aka. NIR lowering in zink and d3d12 (both OpenGL and VA-API).\r\n### Feedback info\r\n- Windows 7 / Server 2008 R2 support remained in place for the time being as [this poll results](https://github.com/pal1000/mesa-dist-win/discussions/112) were 71% in favor of keeping support at release time.\r\n### Known issue \r\n- d3d12 driver build with video acceleration enabled regressed with MSVC and GCC compilers causing VA-API, OpenGL and vulkan software rendering to be unavailable on MSVC and MinGW 32-bit. Workaround by either using MinGW x64 build or [mmozeiko build](https://github.com/mmozeiko/build-mesa/tags) which doesn't have d3d12 video acceleration enabled.\r\n### Build script\r\n- mingw32 pyyaml: Support update from other MSYS2 prefixes.\r\n### Build environment updates\r\n- [MSVC](https://github.com/pal1000/mesa-dist-win/compare/26.2.5..26.2.6#diff-b4e71060df4527250a4a5597da15a5a7cddc32d054cb84a34e5b617ab5855b56)\r\n- [MSYS2 MinGW-w64](https://github.com/pal1000/mesa-dist-win/compare/26.2.5..26.2.6#diff-b2f0f98cfb30e2c28e1ffa79af21ddc4844345657e8ad07028bfe562d7a2fda7)"
}
